### Added

- An explicit-state model of the scratch lifecycle (ompkit-cdll7, VFY-SCRATCH1): `tests/scripts/scratch_lifecycle_model_test.py` copies the guards of `scratch new`, `scratch release` (every `--bin`/`--ref`/`--now` form), `scratch use`/`unuse`, the `scratch apply` sweep and quarantine expiry, and every tree removal (with its chmod-then-retry) from `src/scratch.ts`, citing each line. It explores every reachable state from seven creatable kinds of owned dir (seated and unseated `scratch new`, kitlib temp in a root and nested, the fleet-guard seat dir with and without agent/session, another agent's dir), with writable, read-only and optionally immutable content. It reports each state from which no sequence of owner commands retires the dir, with its shortest trace and whether the reaper still removes it while the owner lives, and two safety findings: an unseated `scratch new` dir that `scratch apply` reaps while its job runs, and an evidence or promote dir that the reaper deletes after content was written into it after its release. Two variants: replaying 0.2.74's plain `rmSync` delete reproduces the read-only export that `release --now` left without its owner record (class D4), and immutable content shows the D4 that HEAD's whole-tree removes still leave. A planted `release --now --bin X` on an unbinned marker shows that the unbinned dead end disappears. Run `python3 tests/scripts/scratch_lifecycle_model_test.py`, or add `--all` to list every state.
